<%# locals: () %>
<%# The way back to the unnarrowed billings list.

    Its own id, because it must be able to ARRIVE ON ITS OWN: its existence
    depends on the search, and the search targets the list frame while this
    link sits outside it. One of BILLING_FRAME_DEPENDENT_REGIONS.

    ⚠️ Unlike the time list, this leads to the BARE named route. The time
    list's bare address re-applies two narrowing defaults, which is why its
    reset carries LIST_NEUTRAL_DRILLDOWN_PARAMS; the billings defaults are
    'all' status and 'all' period, so here the bare address IS the neutral
    list and billing_filter_narrowed? is the whole offering rule. %>
<span id="billing_filter_reset" class="ml-auto">
  <% if billing_filter_narrowed?(@current_billing_status, @effective_date_range) %>
    <%= link_to t('views.organisations.time_session_groups.index.filter_reset'),
                organisation_time_session_groups_path(@current_organisation),
                data: { turbo_frame: '_top', filter_reset: true },
                class: 'text-sm text-lime-700 hover:text-lime-800 hover:underline underline-offset-2' %>
  <% end %>
</span>
